@martinmamql All those examples are correctly returning 4 instead of sqrt(17). The reason is `x.dtype is tf.int32` and the doc clearly says `Returns : The reduced tensor, of the same dtype as the input_tensor.`. However, the document has typo (sqrt(17)) which needs to be corrected. I raised a PR to correct it in `master` and will be updated in the docs after merging the PR. Thanks!

Alternatively, you can add dtype to the end of `x` as follows. Please check the [gist here](https://colab.sandbox.google.com/gist/jvishnuvardhan/dd17894e65c1d74841c197750734633a/36615.ipynb).
`x = tf.constant([[1, 2, 3], [1, 1, 1]], dtype = tf.float32)`
